{
  "keyPoints": [
    {
      "id": "kp1",
      "hit": true,
      "quote": "the report cannot distinguish that from \"the intended hash was recorded\", so ask for the hash after the first sync and reproduce with a disposable consumer over three syncs"
    },
    {
      "id": "kp2",
      "hit": true,
      "quote": "for refused, held and failed paths (`notWrittenByUs`) it carries the PRIOR manifest entry forward, and omits the path when none exists; only the other branch hashes disk."
    },
    {
      "id": "kp3",
      "hit": true,
      "quote": "Do not hand-repair by writing disk hashes into the manifest: that would turn the next refusal into a silent overwrite."
    },
    {
      "id": "kp4",
      "hit": true,
      "quote": "Gate 2B hashes every manifest entry against disk, so 8/8 green over disagreeing paths predicts those paths are declared overrides (held)"
    },
    {
      "id": "kp5",
      "hit": true,
      "quote": "`upstreamMoved` is computed against the previous receipt, which every sync rewrites with the current upstream hash, so the \"upstream changed, review your override\" warning fires once and then goes silent while the consumer stays on the old version. Fix by comparing against the manifest base"
    },
    {
      "id": "kp6",
      "hit": true,
      "quote": "only the refused-path behaviour is reproduced; other observed states stay open."
    }
  ],
  "traps": [
    {
      "id": "trap1",
      "fell": false,
      "quote": ""
    },
